lesson: 89
title: Multiply, then add or take away
stars: 1
explain: Some problems take two steps: first multiply to find the total of the equal groups, then add or take away.
explain: 3 boxes of 8 pencils and 5 loose pencils make 3 × 8 = 24, then 24 + 5 = 29 pencils.
explain: If 6 of those 24 pencils are given away, 24 − 6 = 18 are left.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing g=2..9 k=2..10 m=1..20 x=7..10
need: m >= 2
need: m < g * k
answer: g * k - m
exercise: {a} buys {g} packs of {t} with {k} {t} in each pack. {a.He} gives {m} {t} to {b}. How many {t} does {a} have left?
exercise: There are {g} boxes of {t}, {k} in each box. {m} {t} are eaten. How many {t} remain?
exercise: {a} has {g} bags with {k} {t} in each bag. {a.He} loses {m} {t}. How many {t} are left?
exercise: A class has {g} tables with {k} chairs at each table. {m} chairs are empty. How many chairs have someone sitting on them?
exercise: {a} plants {g} rows of {k} tulips. Rabbits eat {m} of the tulips. How many tulips are left?
test: After giving {m} {t} to {b}, how many {t} does {a} keep from the {g} boxes of {k} {t} {a.he} had?
test: {b} takes {m} {t} out of the {g} boxes that {a} had filled with {k} {t} each. How many {t} are still in the boxes?
test: A shop gets {g} crates of {k} melons. It sells {m} melons. How many melons does it still have?
test: {a} is {x} years old. {a.He} sticks {k} stickers on each of {g} pages, then peels {m} stickers off. How many stickers are still stuck?
exercise: {a} has {g} bags of {t}. Every bag holds {k} {t}. {a.He} hands out {m} {t} at school. How many {t} are left?
exercise: How many {t} remain if {a} had {g} packs of {k} {t} each and gave away {m} of them?
exercise: {a} fills {g} jars with {k} {t} apiece, then donates {m} {t} to a school in Ohio. How many {t} does {a.he} still have?
exercise: {g} packs, {k} {t} per pack, {m} {t} given away. How many {t} are left?
exercise: In a classroom in Toronto there are {g} tables, and every table has {k} pencils on it. The children take {m} pencils. How many pencils are still on the tables?
exercise: {a} bought {g} boxes of {t}, {k} in every box. {a.He} lost {m} {t} on the way home. How many {t} does {a.he} have now?
exercise: A farmer in Kent plants {g} rows of {k} cabbages and picks {m} of them. How many cabbages are not picked?
exercise: {a} owns {g} albums with {k} {t} in each album. {a.He} gives {b} {m} of them. How many {t} remain with {a}?
test: {m} of {a}'s {t} went to {b}. Before that, {a} had {g} sets of {k} {t}. How many {t} does {a} have left?
test: How many seats are still free on a bus in Dublin with {g} rows of {k} seats if {m} people get on?
test: A baker in Sydney makes {g} trays of {k} muffins and sells {m} muffins by noon. How many muffins are not sold yet?
test: {a} had {g} piles of {t}, with {k} {t} in every pile; then {m} {t} were handed out. How many {t} remain?
test: Starting with {g} packets that hold {k} {t} each, {a} passes {m} {t} to friends. How many {t} has {a.he} got now?
test: {a}, aged {x}, sets out {g} rows of {k} chairs in a hall in Auckland. {m} chairs are taken away again. How many chairs stay in the hall?
exercise: {a} got {g+1} packs — no wait, {g} packs of {k} {t}, gave {b} {m}. how many {a.he} got left then
exercise: {g} boxes of {t}, {k} in each, then {b} nicked {m} of em lol. how many left
exercise: {b} says it's {g*k+m} {t} left. nah — {g} bags of {k}, {m} gone. whats the real answer
exercise: so {a}'s got {g} packs of {k} {t}, and {a.he}'s {x} btw, gives {m} away. how many {t} {a.he} got now
test: {g} trays, {k} {t} a tray, {m+1} dropped, no sorry, {m} dropped. how many still on the trays
test: mum bought {g} packs, {k} in each innit, {m} of em are gone already. how many {t} left
test: {a} reckons {g} lots of {k} take away {m} is {g*k-m+10}?? whats it really
exam: It is given that {a} acquired {g} packs of {t}, each pack containing {k} {t}, and subsequently transferred {m} {t} to {b}. Determine the number of {t} remaining in the possession of {a}.
exam: A quantity of {k} {t} is placed in each of {g} boxes, whereupon {m} {t} are removed. Ascertain the number of {t} which remain in the boxes.
exam: Whereas a consignment comprises {g.words} crates of {k} melons apiece, and {m} melons have subsequently been disposed of by sale, state the number of melons still held.
exam: Compute the residual quantity of chairs in a hall wherein {g} rows of {k} chairs were arranged, given that {m} chairs were thereafter withdrawn.
exercise: {a} buys {g} packs of {t} with {k} {t} in each pack. {b} has sticky fingers, and {m} {t} quietly disappear. How many {t} does {a} have left?
exercise: A shop has {g} boxes of {t}, {k} in each. The manager calls the {m} stolen {t} "shrinkage". How many {t} are really left in the shop?
test: {g} packs of {k} {t} and that little terror {b} "borrowed" {m}. borrowed, yeah right. how many have i got left, bloody hell
